WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.940
Welcome to the Federal Modernization
Workbook's developer workbook,

2
00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.287
Building the Attribute-Driven Migration.

3
00:00:06.287 --> 00:00:10.500
This is Chapter 5: Lifecycle
Workflows custom extensions.

4
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.052
A custom task extension hands a leaver,
a joiner or a mover to code you wrote,

5
00:00:15.052 --> 00:00:18.037
and then waits for that
code to say what happened.

6
00:00:18.037 --> 00:00:20.467
The chapter makes sure it always says,

7
00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:23.288
says the truth, and says
it to the right cloud.

8
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:27.328
We'll start from the Logic App
definition Microsoft publishes,

9
00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:30.668
see what it leaves to you,
walk the program's Logic App,

10
00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:33.776
registry and tools, then
two labs and the dangers.

11
00:00:33.776 --> 00:00:38.980
One note before we begin: the code is
illustrative, tested against fixtures.
